  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "Graveyard Keeper 2",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/22343/450x258/graveyard-keeper-2-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791374400",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/22343-buy-graveyard-keeper-2-pc-steam/",
      "user": "Meg",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/9722274-1611493860.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Encore plus de mécanique que dans le 1, énormément de quêtes à faire, on ne s'ennuie pas ! \n\n\n\nLe doublage est excellent XD\n\n\n\nJe recommande fortement !"
    },
    {
      "game": "Tactics Ogre : Reborn",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/12203/450x258/tactics-ogre-reborn-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791374400",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/12203-buy-tactics-ogre-reborn-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Ken2045",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "If you are a fan of tactical RPGs, Tactics Ogre: Reborn is not just a game you should play—it is an absolute essential experience. Building upon the legendary foundation of the original tactical classic, this definitive version elevates the genre to new heights, offering a masterclass in strategic depth, storytelling, and world-building."
    },
    {
      "game": "Graveyard Keeper 2",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/22343/450x258/graveyard-keeper-2-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791374400",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/22343-buy-graveyard-keeper-2-pc-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-7cdec8e",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Very addicting, but late game is grindy and a lot of stuff isn't explained to you.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately, the graveyard feels more like a second thought now. The game's story is more focused on helping rebuild the town and the new 'tower defender' mini game.\n\n\n\nThe game can be buggy at times. I have gotten myself softlocked by the most stupid things...Placing a building item too close to each other, walking too far at the docks (there is an invisible wall, that prevents you from going back lol), among other bugs that need to be fixed. If you play it on PC, you won't have much issues like our console fellows.\n\n\n\nThe zombie factory part should be fixed more and the devs have released plans on changing and fixing this, so I am hopeful.\n\n\n\nIf you liked the first one, I would still recommend GK2!"
    },
    {
      "game": "Crashout Crew",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/20607/450x258/crashout-crew-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791374400",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/20607-buy-crashout-crew-pc-steam/",
      "user": "Nox",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/20119100-1677546338.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "It's alright, it feels like overcooked but with a warehouse. If you're coming from Peak, IMO while it is more polished it is also more \"limited\" and you'll quick get the whole it has to offer even before you finish all the levels, still had some fun worth it it's price for sure."
    }
  ],
